# WARLOG behind HTTPS (RBAC Phase 8, H8) - Caddy reverse proxy.
#
# 1. Install Caddy (https://caddyserver.com/docs/install) on the WARLOG PC.
# 2. In .env set:   HOST=127.0.0.1        (Waitress only reachable through Caddy)
#                   BEHIND_TLS_PROXY=1    (secure cookies, real client IP, HSTS)
#                   APP_BASE_URL=https://<the address below>/
# 3. Pick ONE of the two site blocks below, then run:  caddy run --config deploy/Caddyfile
#
# A) With a domain name pointing at this PC (automatic Let's Encrypt certificate):
#
# warlog.example.com {
#     encode gzip
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000 {
#         flush_interval -1          # live MJPEG camera streams must not be buffered
#     }
# }
#
# B) Warehouse LAN without a domain (Caddy's own certificate; install Caddy's root
#    certificate once on each device with `caddy trust`, or accept the browser prompt):

https://{$WARLOG_LAN_IP:192.168.1.10} {
    tls internal
    encode gzip
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000 {
        flush_interval -1
    }
}

# Plain HTTP on the LAN redirects to HTTPS.
http://{$WARLOG_LAN_IP:192.168.1.10} {
    redir https://{host}{uri} permanent
}
